# - resource -------------------------------------------------------------------

<https://YasniiSS.github.io/fhir4eyes/CodeSystem/fhir4eyes-cs> a fhir:CodeSystem ;
  fhir:nodeRole fhir:treeRoot ;
  fhir:Resource.id [ fhir:value "fhir4eyes-cs"] ;
  fhir:DomainResource.text [
     fhir:Narrative.status [ fhir:value "generated" ] ;
     fhir:Narrative.div "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: CodeSystem fhir4eyes-cs</b></p><a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs\"> </a><a name=\"hcfhir4eyes-cs\"> </a><p>This case-sensitive code system <code>https://YasniiSS.github.io/fhir4eyes/CodeSystem/fhir4eyes-cs</code> defines the following codes:</p><table class=\"codes\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">central-corneal-thickness<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-central-corneal-thickness\"> </a></td><td>Central corneal thickness</td><td>Central corneal thickness, independent of the eye measured. Eye-specific LOINC: 79825-6 (right) / 79826-4 (left).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">specular-microscopy-panel<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-specular-microscopy-panel\"> </a></td><td>Corneal endothelial specular microscopy</td><td>Panel code for a corneal endothelial specular microscopy exam.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">specular-capture-position<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-specular-capture-position\"> </a></td><td>Specular microscopy capture position</td><td>Location of the corneal capture (central, paracentral, peripheral).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">specular-analysis-method<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-specular-analysis-method\"> </a></td><td>Specular microscopy analysis method</td><td>Type of analysis method. Eye-specific LOINC: 100086-8 (right) / 100155-1 (left).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">endothelial-cell-density<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-endothelial-cell-density\"> </a></td><td>Corneal endothelial cell density</td><td>Eye-specific LOINC: 100070-2 (right) / 100071-0 (left).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">endothelial-cells-counted<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-endothelial-cells-counted\"> </a></td><td>Corneal endothelial cells counted</td><td>Eye-specific LOINC: 100076-9 (right) / 100077-7 (left).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">endothelial-cell-area-cv<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-endothelial-cell-area-cv\"> </a></td><td>Corneal endothelial cell area coefficient of variation</td><td>Eye-specific LOINC: 100072-8 (right) / 100073-6 (left).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">endothelial-hexagonality<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-endothelial-hexagonality\"> </a></td><td>Corneal endothelial hexagonality</td><td>Eye-specific LOINC: 100074-4 (right) / 100075-1 (left).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">endothelial-cell-area-min<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-endothelial-cell-area-min\"> </a></td><td>Corneal endothelial cell area, minimum</td><td>Eye-specific LOINC: 100078-5 (right) / 100079-3 (left).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">endothelial-cell-area-max<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-endothelial-cell-area-max\"> </a></td><td>Corneal endothelial cell area, maximum</td><td>Eye-specific LOINC: 100080-1 (right) / 100081-9 (left).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">endothelial-cell-area-mean<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-endothelial-cell-area-mean\"> </a></td><td>Corneal endothelial cell area, mean</td><td>Eye-specific LOINC: 100082-7 (right) / 100083-5 (left).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">endothelial-cell-area-sd<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-endothelial-cell-area-sd\"> </a></td><td>Corneal endothelial cell area, standard deviation</td><td>Eye-specific LOINC: 100084-3 (right) / 100085-0 (left).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">axial-length<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-axial-length\"> </a></td><td>Axial length</td><td>Anteroposterior length of the eye (corneal vertex to retina/RPE), e.g. by optical or ultrasound biometry.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">anterior-chamber-depth<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-anterior-chamber-depth\"> </a></td><td>Anterior chamber depth</td><td>Distance from the cornea to the anterior lens surface.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">lens-thickness<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-lens-thickness\"> </a></td><td>Lens thickness</td><td>Axial thickness of the crystalline lens.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">white-to-white<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-white-to-white\"> </a></td><td>White-to-white corneal diameter</td><td>Horizontal visible corneal diameter (limbus to limbus).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">keratometry-k1<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-keratometry-k1\"> </a></td><td>Keratometry K1 (flat)</td><td>Corneal power of the flattest meridian of the anterior corneal surface, in dioptres.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">keratometry-k2<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-keratometry-k2\"> </a></td><td>Keratometry K2 (steep)</td><td>Corneal power of the steepest meridian of the anterior corneal surface, in dioptres.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">keratometry-k1-radius<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-keratometry-k1-radius\"> </a></td><td>Keratometry K1 radius of curvature</td><td>Radius of curvature of the flattest meridian of the anterior corneal surface, in millimetres.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">keratometry-k2-radius<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-keratometry-k2-radius\"> </a></td><td>Keratometry K2 radius of curvature</td><td>Radius of curvature of the steepest meridian of the anterior corneal surface, in millimetres.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-astigmatism<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-astigmatism\"> </a></td><td>Corneal astigmatism (cylinder)</td><td>Corneal (keratometric) astigmatism, the difference between steep and flat meridian powers (K2 - K1) in dioptres, reported as a positive magnitude (plus-cylinder notation) at the steep meridian.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">keratometric-index<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-keratometric-index\"> </a></td><td>Keratometric index</td><td>Refractive index used to convert corneal radius of curvature into corneal power (e.g. 1.3375).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">pupil-diameter<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-pupil-diameter\"> </a></td><td>Pupil diameter</td><td>Diameter of the pupil at the time of the measurement.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">pupil-dilated<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-pupil-dilated\"> </a></td><td>Pupil dilated</td><td>Whether the pupil was pharmacologically dilated at the time of the measurement.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">mydriatic-agent<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-mydriatic-agent\"> </a></td><td>Mydriatic agent</td><td>Mydriatic agent used to dilate the pupil, if any.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">test-distance<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-test-distance\"> </a></td><td>Testing distance</td><td>Distance between the patient and the test target (chart, fixation target) during the test, as a measured quantity. For a near/far category use test-distance-category.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">correction-status<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-correction-status\"> </a></td><td>Refractive correction status during test</td><td>Whether the test was performed with or without the patient's refractive correction.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">ocular-biometry<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-ocular-biometry\"> </a></td><td>Ocular biometry</td><td>Panel code for an ocular biometry exam (optical or ultrasound), typically for IOL power calculation. Formula results are separate IOL formula result observations.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">axial-length-measurement-type<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-axial-length-measurement-type\"> </a></td><td>Axial length measurement type</td><td>Technique used to measure axial length: optical, ultrasound immersion or ultrasound contact.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">axial-length-snr<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-axial-length-snr\"> </a></td><td>Axial length signal-to-noise ratio</td><td>Signal-to-noise ratio of the optical axial length measurement, a quality indicator.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">axial-length-selection-method<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-axial-length-selection-method\"> </a></td><td>Axial length selection method</td><td>Method used to select the reported axial length from multiple measurements.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">anterior-chamber-depth-definition<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-anterior-chamber-depth-definition\"> </a></td><td>Anterior chamber depth definition</td><td>Reference surfaces used for the ACD measurement (corneal epithelium or endothelium to anterior lens).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">lens-status<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-lens-status\"> </a></td><td>Lens status</td><td>Status of the crystalline lens: phakic, pseudophakic or aphakic.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">vitreous-status<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-vitreous-status\"> </a></td><td>Vitreous status</td><td>Status of the vitreous body, relevant to the sound velocity used in ultrasound biometry.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">keratometry-mean-radius<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-keratometry-mean-radius\"> </a></td><td>Keratometry mean radius of curvature (R/SE)</td><td>Mean radius of curvature of the anterior corneal surface in mm, (K1 radius + K2 radius)/2, as reported in the R part of the biometer R/SE field. The dioptric mean (SE) is keratometry-km.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">refractive-surgery-history<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-refractive-surgery-history\"> </a></td><td>Refractive surgery history</td><td>Prior corneal or refractive surgery of the eye, critical for IOL formula selection.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">target-refraction<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-target-refraction\"> </a></td><td>Target refraction</td><td>Desired postoperative refraction used for IOL power calculation.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">refractive-error-type<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-refractive-error-type\"> </a></td><td>Refractive error type</td><td>Type of refractive error of the eye.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">measurement-data-source<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-measurement-data-source\"> </a></td><td>Measurement data source</td><td>Origin of the biometry measurement data (e.g. automatic, manually entered, from another device).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">vertex-distance<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-vertex-distance\"> </a></td><td>Vertex distance</td><td>Distance between the back surface of a spectacle lens and the corneal apex.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">iol-formula-result<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-iol-formula-result\"> </a></td><td>IOL power calculation formula result</td><td>Panel code for the result of one IOL power calculation formula applied to an ocular biometry exam.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">iol-formula<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-iol-formula\"> </a></td><td>IOL power calculation formula</td><td>Formula used for the IOL power calculation (e.g. Barrett Universal II, SRK/T, Holladay 2, Kane).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">iol-lens-constant-type<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-iol-lens-constant-type\"> </a></td><td>IOL lens constant type</td><td>Type of IOL optimization constant (e.g. A-constant, surgeon factor, ACD constant).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">iol-lens-constant-value<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-iol-lens-constant-value\"> </a></td><td>IOL lens constant value</td><td>Value of the IOL optimization constant used for the calculation.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">iol-model<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-iol-model\"> </a></td><td>Suggested IOL model</td><td>Intraocular lens model suggested by this formula calculation.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">iol-power<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-iol-power\"> </a></td><td>Recommended IOL power</td><td>IOL power, in dioptres, recommended by this formula calculation.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">iol-expected-refraction<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-iol-expected-refraction\"> </a></td><td>Predicted postoperative refraction</td><td>Refraction predicted by the formula for the recommended IOL power.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">iol-power-table<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-iol-power-table\"> </a></td><td>IOL power table</td><td>Range of IOL powers with the predicted refraction for each, as listed in the biometry report for this formula.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">visual-acuity-scale<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-visual-acuity-scale\"> </a></td><td>Visual acuity notation scale</td><td>Notation in which the visual acuity value is expressed (e.g. Snellen fraction, decimal, LogMAR).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">pinhole-used<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-pinhole-used\"> </a></td><td>Pinhole occluder used</td><td>Whether the visual acuity measurement was taken through a pinhole occluder.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corrected-intraocular-pressure<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corrected-intraocular-pressure\"> </a></td><td>Intraocular pressure corrected for central corneal thickness</td><td>Intraocular pressure adjusted for central corneal thickness, derived from an IOP reading and a pachymetry measurement. LOINC 96093-0/96092-2 (compensated IOP) exist but may not be equivalent to CCT-based correction; not used.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">tension-curve<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-tension-curve\"> </a></td><td>Diurnal intraocular pressure tension curve</td><td>Panel grouping several intraocular pressure readings taken across a single day (diurnal / ambulatory tension curve).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-tomography-anterior-surface<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-tomography-anterior-surface\"> </a></td><td>Corneal tomography, anterior surface analysis</td><td>Anterior corneal surface analysis component of a corneal tomography exam.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">keratometry-kmax<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-keratometry-kmax\"> </a></td><td>Maximum keratometry (Kmax)</td><td>Maximum keratometric power on the anterior corneal surface; key parameter for keratoconus detection and progression.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">simulated-keratometry<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-simulated-keratometry\"> </a></td><td>Simulated keratometry (SimK)</td><td>Simulated keratometry values (steep/flat) derived from the topographic/tomographic map.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-radius-horizontal<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-radius-horizontal\"> </a></td><td>Horizontal corneal radius of curvature (Rh)</td><td>Corneal radius of curvature along the horizontal (0-180 degree) meridian; not necessarily a principal (K1/K2) meridian.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-radius-vertical<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-radius-vertical\"> </a></td><td>Vertical corneal radius of curvature (Rv)</td><td>Corneal radius of curvature along the vertical (90 degree) meridian; not necessarily a principal (K1/K2) meridian.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-asphericity-q-anterior<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-asphericity-q-anterior\"> </a></td><td>Corneal asphericity (Q-value), anterior surface</td><td>Asphericity (Q-value) of the anterior corneal surface; typical normal value about -0.26.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">elevation-anterior<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-elevation-anterior\"> </a></td><td>Corneal elevation relative to best fit sphere, anterior surface</td><td>Elevation of the anterior corneal surface relative to its best fit sphere.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">best-fit-sphere-radius-anterior<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-best-fit-sphere-radius-anterior\"> </a></td><td>Best fit sphere radius, anterior surface</td><td>Radius of the best fit sphere of the anterior corneal surface.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">surface-regularity-index<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-surface-regularity-index\"> </a></td><td>Surface Regularity Index (SRI)</td><td>Topographic index of local corneal surface regularity within the central zone.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">surface-asymmetry-index<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-surface-asymmetry-index\"> </a></td><td>Surface Asymmetry Index (SAI)</td><td>Topographic index of corneal power asymmetry between opposite hemimeridians.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">inferior-superior-asymmetry<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-inferior-superior-asymmetry\"> </a></td><td>Inferior-superior asymmetry value (I-S)</td><td>Difference in mean corneal power between inferior and superior regions; keratoconus screening value.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">kisa-index<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-kisa-index\"> </a></td><td>KISA% index</td><td>KISA% keratoconus screening index combining central K, I-S value, astigmatism and skewed radial axis.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">topographic-pattern<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-topographic-pattern\"> </a></td><td>Topographic pattern</td><td>Classification of the corneal topographic map pattern (regular, irregular, keratoconus, pellucid, post-LASIK, forme fruste).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">total-corneal-refractive-power<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-total-corneal-refractive-power\"> </a></td><td>Total corneal refractive power (TCRP)</td><td>Total corneal refractive power calculated by ray tracing through anterior and posterior corneal surfaces.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">true-net-power<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-true-net-power\"> </a></td><td>True net corneal power (TNP)</td><td>True net corneal power calculated from anterior and posterior corneal curvature using Gaussian optics.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">equivalent-keratometry-1mm<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-equivalent-keratometry-1mm\"> </a></td><td>Equivalent K reading (EKR), 1.0 mm zone</td><td>Holladay equivalent keratometry reading over a 1.0 mm zone.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">equivalent-keratometry-3mm<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-equivalent-keratometry-3mm\"> </a></td><td>Equivalent K reading (EKR), 3.0 mm zone</td><td>Holladay equivalent keratometry reading over a 3.0 mm zone.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">equivalent-keratometry-4-5mm<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-equivalent-keratometry-4-5mm\"> </a></td><td>Equivalent K reading (EKR), 4.5 mm zone</td><td>Holladay equivalent keratometry reading over a 4.5 mm zone; used for IOL calculation after refractive surgery.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-mean-power-3mm-zone<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-mean-power-3mm-zone\"> </a></td><td>Mean corneal power, 3 mm zone</td><td>Mean corneal power within the central 3 mm zone.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-astigmatism-power-3mm-zone<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-astigmatism-power-3mm-zone\"> </a></td><td>Corneal astigmatism power, 3 mm zone</td><td>Corneal astigmatism power within the central 3 mm zone.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-steep-axis-3mm-zone<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-steep-axis-3mm-zone\"> </a></td><td>Corneal steep axis, 3 mm zone</td><td>Steep meridian axis within the central 3 mm zone.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-flat-axis-3mm-zone<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-flat-axis-3mm-zone\"> </a></td><td>Corneal flat axis, 3 mm zone</td><td>Flat meridian axis within the central 3 mm zone.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-mean-power-5mm-zone<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-mean-power-5mm-zone\"> </a></td><td>Mean corneal power, 5 mm zone</td><td>Mean corneal power within the central 5 mm zone.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-astigmatism-power-5mm-zone<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-astigmatism-power-5mm-zone\"> </a></td><td>Corneal astigmatism power, 5 mm zone</td><td>Corneal astigmatism power within the central 5 mm zone.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-steep-axis-5mm-zone<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-steep-axis-5mm-zone\"> </a></td><td>Corneal steep axis, 5 mm zone</td><td>Steep meridian axis within the central 5 mm zone.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-flat-axis-5mm-zone<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-flat-axis-5mm-zone\"> </a></td><td>Corneal flat axis, 5 mm zone</td><td>Flat meridian axis within the central 5 mm zone.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">total-corneal-astigmatism<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-total-corneal-astigmatism\"> </a></td><td>Total corneal astigmatism (tWFA)</td><td>Total corneal astigmatism including the posterior surface, derived from corneal wavefront analysis.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-irregular-astigmatism<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-irregular-astigmatism\"> </a></td><td>Total corneal irregular astigmatism</td><td>Higher-order (irregular) component of total corneal astigmatism.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-hoa-rms<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-hoa-rms\"> </a></td><td>Corneal higher-order aberrations RMS</td><td>Root mean square of corneal higher-order wavefront aberrations.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">angle-kappa<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-angle-kappa\"> </a></td><td>Angle kappa</td><td>Angle between the visual axis and the pupillary axis.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">angle-kappa-intercept<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-angle-kappa-intercept\"> </a></td><td>Angle kappa intercept</td><td>Coordinates (x,y) of the angle kappa intercept relative to the pupil centre.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">surgically-induced-astigmatism<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-surgically-induced-astigmatism\"> </a></td><td>Surgically induced astigmatism (SIA)</td><td>Expected corneal astigmatism induced by the surgical incision, used in surgical planning.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">predicted-postoperative-corneal-astigmatism<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-predicted-postoperative-corneal-astigmatism\"> </a></td><td>Predicted postoperative corneal astigmatism</td><td>Expected residual corneal astigmatism after surgery, used in toric IOL planning.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">toric-iol-optimal-axis<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-toric-iol-optimal-axis\"> </a></td><td>Optimal toric IOL axis</td><td>Recommended implantation axis for a toric intraocular lens.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-vertex-location<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-vertex-location\"> </a></td><td>Corneal vertex location</td><td>Position coordinates of the corneal vertex.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">pupil-centroid-x<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-pupil-centroid-x\"> </a></td><td>Pupil centroid X coordinate</td><td>X-coordinate of the pupil centre.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">pupil-centroid-y<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-pupil-centroid-y\"> </a></td><td>Pupil centroid Y coordinate</td><td>Y-coordinate of the pupil centre.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">equivalent-pupil-radius<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-equivalent-pupil-radius\"> </a></td><td>Equivalent pupil radius</td><td>Radius of the equivalent circular pupil.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-topography-map-type<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-topography-map-type\"> </a></td><td>Corneal topography map type</td><td>Type of topographic map encoded (axial, tangential, elevation, refractive, pachymetry).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-analyzed-area<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-analyzed-area\"> </a></td><td>Corneal analyzed area</td><td>Total area of the cornea analyzed.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-eccentricity-index<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-eccentricity-index\"> </a></td><td>Corneal eccentricity index</td><td>Corneal eccentricity (shape factor).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">keratoconus-prediction-index<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-keratoconus-prediction-index\"> </a></td><td>Keratoconus prediction index (KPI)</td><td>Corneal keratoconus prediction index, distinct from KISA%.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">potential-visual-acuity-decimal<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-potential-visual-acuity-decimal\"> </a></td><td>Decimal potential visual acuity</td><td>Estimated potential visual acuity (decimal) from the corneal surface.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-tomography-posterior-surface<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-tomography-posterior-surface\"> </a></td><td>Corneal tomography, posterior surface analysis</td><td>Posterior corneal surface analysis component of a corneal tomography exam.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">posterior-keratometry-k1<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-posterior-keratometry-k1\"> </a></td><td>Posterior keratometry K1 (flat)</td><td>Keratometric power of the flattest meridian of the posterior corneal surface; a negative value in dioptres.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">posterior-keratometry-k2<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-posterior-keratometry-k2\"> </a></td><td>Posterior keratometry K2 (steep)</td><td>Keratometric power of the steepest meridian of the posterior corneal surface; a negative value in dioptres.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">posterior-keratometry-km<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-posterior-keratometry-km\"> </a></td><td>Posterior keratometry Km (mean)</td><td>Mean keratometric power of the posterior corneal surface; a negative value in dioptres.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-astigmatism-posterior<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-astigmatism-posterior\"> </a></td><td>Corneal astigmatism, posterior surface</td><td>Astigmatism of the posterior corneal surface, reported as a positive magnitude in dioptres (difference between posterior K2 and K1) with the posterior steep meridian as axis.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-asphericity-q-posterior<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-asphericity-q-posterior\"> </a></td><td>Corneal asphericity (Q-value), posterior surface</td><td>Asphericity (Q-value) of the posterior corneal surface.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">elevation-posterior<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-elevation-posterior\"> </a></td><td>Corneal elevation relative to best fit sphere, posterior surface</td><td>Elevation of the posterior corneal surface relative to its best fit sphere.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">best-fit-sphere-radius-posterior<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-best-fit-sphere-radius-posterior\"> </a></td><td>Best fit sphere radius, posterior surface</td><td>Radius of the best fit sphere of the posterior corneal surface.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-tomography-pachymetry<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-tomography-pachymetry\"> </a></td><td>Corneal tomography, pachymetry analysis</td><td>Pachymetry (corneal thickness map) component of a corneal tomography exam.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-thickness-pupil-centre<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-thickness-pupil-centre\"> </a></td><td>Corneal thickness at pupil centre</td><td>Corneal thickness measured at the pupil centre; may differ from the thickness at the corneal apex.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-thickness-thinnest<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-thickness-thinnest\"> </a></td><td>Thinnest corneal thickness</td><td>Corneal thickness at the thinnest point of the pachymetry map.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-thinnest-point-location<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-thinnest-point-location\"> </a></td><td>Thinnest corneal point location</td><td>Location (x,y) of the thinnest corneal point relative to the reference centre.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-volume<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-volume\"> </a></td><td>Corneal volume</td><td>Total corneal volume within the analysed diameter.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-tomography-anterior-chamber<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-tomography-anterior-chamber\"> </a></td><td>Corneal tomography, anterior chamber analysis</td><td>Anterior chamber analysis component of a corneal tomography exam.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">anterior-chamber-volume<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-anterior-chamber-volume\"> </a></td><td>Anterior chamber volume</td><td>Volume of the anterior chamber.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">anterior-chamber-angle<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-anterior-chamber-angle\"> </a></td><td>Anterior chamber angle</td><td>Iridocorneal (anterior chamber) angle width in degrees, as measured by the tomographer.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">keratoconus-indices<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-keratoconus-indices\"> </a></td><td>Keratoconus indices</td><td>Keratoconus screening and classification indices component of a corneal tomography exam.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bad-d<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-bad-d\"> </a></td><td>Belin-Ambrosio total deviation (BAD-D)</td><td>Final overall deviation index (D) of the Belin-Ambrosio Enhanced Ectasia Display; key keratoconus screening index.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bad-df<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-bad-df\"> </a></td><td>Belin-Ambrosio front elevation deviation (Df)</td><td>Deviation of anterior elevation relative to the enhanced best fit sphere (BAD component Df).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bad-db<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-bad-db\"> </a></td><td>Belin-Ambrosio back elevation deviation (Db)</td><td>Deviation of posterior elevation relative to the enhanced best fit sphere (BAD component Db).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bad-dt<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-bad-dt\"> </a></td><td>Belin-Ambrosio thinnest point deviation (Dt)</td><td>Deviation of the thinnest corneal thickness from normal (BAD component Dt).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bad-dy<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-bad-dy\"> </a></td><td>Belin-Ambrosio vertical asymmetry deviation (Dy)</td><td>Deviation of the Y-coordinate (vertical displacement) of the thinnest point (BAD component Dy).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">bad-classification<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-bad-classification\"> </a></td><td>Belin-Ambrosio classification</td><td>Classification of the Belin-Ambrosio display result (normal, suspicious, abnormal).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">enhanced-best-fit-sphere-radius-anterior<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-enhanced-best-fit-sphere-radius-anterior\"> </a></td><td>Enhanced best fit sphere radius, anterior surface</td><td>Radius of the enhanced best fit sphere of the anterior corneal surface (BAD enhanced reference).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">enhanced-best-fit-sphere-radius-posterior<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-enhanced-best-fit-sphere-radius-posterior\"> </a></td><td>Enhanced best fit sphere radius, posterior surface</td><td>Radius of the enhanced best fit sphere of the posterior corneal surface (BAD enhanced reference).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">amsler-krumeich-stage<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-amsler-krumeich-stage\"> </a></td><td>Amsler-Krumeich keratoconus stage</td><td>Classic Amsler-Krumeich keratoconus staging (I-IV).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">belin-abcd-grade<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-belin-abcd-grade\"> </a></td><td>Belin ABCD keratoconus grade</td><td>Belin ABCD keratoconus grading (anterior and posterior radius of curvature, thinnest pachymetry, distance visual acuity).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">index-surface-variance<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-index-surface-variance\"> </a></td><td>Index of surface variance (ISV)</td><td>Topometric index of the deviation of individual corneal radii from the mean.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">index-vertical-asymmetry<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-index-vertical-asymmetry\"> </a></td><td>Index of vertical asymmetry (IVA)</td><td>Topometric index of superior-inferior corneal curvature asymmetry.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">keratoconus-index<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-keratoconus-index\"> </a></td><td>Keratoconus index (KI)</td><td>Topometric ratio of central to peripheral corneal curvature.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">center-keratoconus-index<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-center-keratoconus-index\"> </a></td><td>Center keratoconus index (CKI)</td><td>Topometric central corneal curvature index.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">index-height-asymmetry<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-index-height-asymmetry\"> </a></td><td>Index of height asymmetry (IHA)</td><td>Topometric index of superior-inferior corneal elevation asymmetry.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">index-height-decentration<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-index-height-decentration\"> </a></td><td>Index of height decentration (IHD)</td><td>Topometric index of the degree of vertical decentration of corneal elevation.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">topographic-keratoconus-classification<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-topographic-keratoconus-classification\"> </a></td><td>Topographic keratoconus classification (TKC)</td><td>Automated topographic keratoconus classification provided by the tomographer.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-densitometry<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-densitometry\"> </a></td><td>Corneal densitometry</td><td>Corneal densitometry (light backscatter) component of a corneal tomography exam.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-densitometry-zone-0-2mm<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-densitometry-zone-0-2mm\"> </a></td><td>Corneal densitometry, 0-2 mm zone</td><td>Corneal light backscatter (densitometry, grayscale units) in the central 0-2 mm annular zone.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-densitometry-zone-2-6mm<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-densitometry-zone-2-6mm\"> </a></td><td>Corneal densitometry, 2-6 mm zone</td><td>Corneal light backscatter (densitometry, grayscale units) in the paracentral 2-6 mm annular zone.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-densitometry-zone-6-10mm<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-densitometry-zone-6-10mm\"> </a></td><td>Corneal densitometry, 6-10 mm zone</td><td>Corneal light backscatter (densitometry, grayscale units) in the peripheral 6-10 mm annular zone.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-densitometry-total<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-densitometry-total\"> </a></td><td>Corneal densitometry, total</td><td>Overall corneal light backscatter (densitometry, grayscale units).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-densitometry-anterior-layer<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-densitometry-anterior-layer\"> </a></td><td>Corneal densitometry, anterior layer</td><td>Corneal light backscatter (densitometry, grayscale units) of the anterior 120 um layer.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-densitometry-central-layer<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-densitometry-central-layer\"> </a></td><td>Corneal densitometry, central layer</td><td>Corneal light backscatter (densitometry, grayscale units) of the central stromal layer.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-densitometry-posterior-layer<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-densitometry-posterior-layer\"> </a></td><td>Corneal densitometry, posterior layer</td><td>Corneal light backscatter (densitometry, grayscale units) of the posterior 60 um layer.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">keratometry-k1-axis<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-keratometry-k1-axis\"> </a></td><td>Keratometry K1 axis</td><td>Orientation of the flat meridian.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">keratometry-k2-axis<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-keratometry-k2-axis\"> </a></td><td>Keratometry K2 axis</td><td>Orientation of the steep meridian.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">keratometry-km<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-keratometry-km\"> </a></td><td>Keratometry Km (mean)</td><td>Mean keratometry, (K1+K2)/2.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">pachymetric-progression<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-pachymetric-progression\"> </a></td><td>Pachymetric progression index (BAD Dp)</td><td>Rate of corneal thickness increase from the thinnest point toward the periphery; the pachymetric progression deviation (Dp) of the Belin-Ambrosio display.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">radius-minimum-curvature<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-radius-minimum-curvature\"> </a></td><td>Minimum radius of curvature (Rmin)</td><td>Radius of curvature at the steepest point of the corneal surface.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">radius-minimum-sagittal<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-radius-minimum-sagittal\"> </a></td><td>Minimum sagittal radius of curvature (Rmin)</td><td>Minimum radius of sagittal (axial) curvature, i.e. the steepest point of the sagittal curvature map (Pentacam topometric index Rmin).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">signal-strength<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-signal-strength\"> </a></td><td>Scan signal strength / quality</td><td>Device-reported scan signal strength or quality score.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">retinal-thickness-definition<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-retinal-thickness-definition\"> </a></td><td>Retinal thickness definition</td><td>Boundaries used to define a retinal or RNFL thickness measurement (e.g. ILM to RPE, ILM to Bruch's membrane, ILM to RNFL outer boundary).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">normative-deviation-category<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-normative-deviation-category\"> </a></td><td>Normative database deviation category</td><td>Classification of a measurement against the device normative database (e.g. within normal limits, borderline, outside normal limits).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">pupil-dilation-degree<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-pupil-dilation-degree\"> </a></td><td>Degree of pupil dilation</td><td>Degree of pupil dilation, expressed as pupil diameter in mm.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">central-subfield-thickness-min<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-central-subfield-thickness-min\"> </a></td><td>Central subfield thickness, minimum</td><td>Minimum retinal thickness measured within the central (1 mm) ETDRS subfield.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">central-subfield-thickness-max<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-central-subfield-thickness-max\"> </a></td><td>Central subfield thickness, maximum</td><td>Maximum retinal thickness measured within the central (1 mm) ETDRS subfield.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">macular-subfield-volume<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-macular-subfield-volume\"> </a></td><td>Macular ETDRS subfield volume</td><td>Retinal volume of a single ETDRS grid subfield; the subfield is identified by the component context. For the total grid volume use LOINC 57118-2.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">etdrs-grid-diameters<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-etdrs-grid-diameters\"> </a></td><td>ETDRS grid circle diameters</td><td>Diameters of the concentric circles of the ETDRS measurement grid used for the analysis (usually 1, 3 and 6 mm).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">anatomic-reference-point<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-anatomic-reference-point\"> </a></td><td>Ophthalmic anatomic reference point</td><td>Anatomic structure used as the reference point to centre the measurement grid (e.g. fovea, optic disc centre).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">optic-cup-area<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-optic-cup-area\"> </a></td><td>Optic cup area</td><td>Area of the optic cup from optic nerve head analysis, in mm2.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">optic-cup-volume<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-optic-cup-volume\"> </a></td><td>Optic cup volume</td><td>Volume of the optic cup from optic nerve head analysis, in mm3.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">neuroretinal-rim-volume<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-neuroretinal-rim-volume\"> </a></td><td>Neuroretinal rim volume</td><td>Volume of the neuroretinal rim from optic nerve head analysis, in mm3.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">cup-disc-ratio-horizontal<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-cup-disc-ratio-horizontal\"> </a></td><td>Cup-to-disc ratio, horizontal</td><td>Ratio of horizontal optic cup diameter to horizontal optic disc diameter.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">cup-disc-ratio-vertical<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-cup-disc-ratio-vertical\"> </a></td><td>Cup-to-disc ratio, vertical</td><td>Ratio of vertical optic cup diameter to vertical optic disc diameter.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">optic-disc-diameter-horizontal<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-optic-disc-diameter-horizontal\"> </a></td><td>Optic disc diameter, horizontal</td><td>Horizontal diameter of the optic disc, in mm.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">optic-disc-diameter-vertical<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-optic-disc-diameter-vertical\"> </a></td><td>Optic disc diameter, vertical</td><td>Vertical diameter of the optic disc, in mm.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">optic-disc-diameter-mean<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-optic-disc-diameter-mean\"> </a></td><td>Optic disc diameter, mean</td><td>Mean diameter of the optic disc, in mm.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">optic-cup-diameter-horizontal<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-optic-cup-diameter-horizontal\"> </a></td><td>Optic cup diameter, horizontal</td><td>Horizontal diameter of the optic cup, in mm.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">optic-cup-diameter-vertical<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-optic-cup-diameter-vertical\"> </a></td><td>Optic cup diameter, vertical</td><td>Vertical diameter of the optic cup, in mm.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">optic-cup-diameter-mean<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-optic-cup-diameter-mean\"> </a></td><td>Optic cup diameter, mean</td><td>Mean diameter of the optic cup, in mm.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">optic-cup-depth-mean<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-optic-cup-depth-mean\"> </a></td><td>Optic cup depth, mean</td><td>Mean depth of the optic cup from optic nerve head analysis, in mm.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">optic-cup-depth-max<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-optic-cup-depth-max\"> </a></td><td>Optic cup depth, maximum</td><td>Maximum depth of the optic cup from optic nerve head analysis, in mm.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">optic-disc-vertical-horizontal-ratio<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-optic-disc-vertical-horizontal-ratio\"> </a></td><td>Optic disc vertical-to-horizontal diameter ratio</td><td>Ratio of vertical to horizontal optic disc diameter (disc ovality).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">optic-cup-vertical-horizontal-ratio<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-optic-cup-vertical-horizontal-ratio\"> </a></td><td>Optic cup vertical-to-horizontal diameter ratio</td><td>Ratio of vertical to horizontal optic cup diameter.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">rim-disc-area-ratio<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-rim-disc-area-ratio\"> </a></td><td>Neuroretinal rim-to-disc area ratio</td><td>Ratio of neuroretinal rim area to optic disc area.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">neuroretinal-rim-absence-extent<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-neuroretinal-rim-absence-extent\"> </a></td><td>Angular extent of neuroretinal rim absence</td><td>Angular (circumferential) extent, in degrees, over which the neuroretinal rim is absent; input to DDLS staging.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">disc-damage-likelihood-scale<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-disc-damage-likelihood-scale\"> </a></td><td>Disc Damage Likelihood Scale (DDLS) stage</td><td>Disc Damage Likelihood Scale stage (1-10), based on the narrowest rim width or angular extent of rim absence, adjusted for disc size.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">rnfl-symmetry<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-rnfl-symmetry\"> </a></td><td>RNFL inter-eye symmetry</td><td>Symmetry of the RNFL thickness profile between right and left eyes (e.g. Cirrus RNFL symmetry).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">rnfl-thickness-mean-tsnit<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-rnfl-thickness-mean-tsnit\"> </a></td><td>Mean RNFL thickness (TSNIT average)</td><td>Average peripapillary RNFL thickness across the temporal-superior-nasal-inferior-temporal (TSNIT) profile, laterality-neutral. Instances may add an eye-specific LOINC as an optional second coding (candidates 86301-9 right / 86290-4 left, to be verified).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">rnfl-thickness-tsnit-sd<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-rnfl-thickness-tsnit-sd\"> </a></td><td>RNFL TSNIT profile standard deviation</td><td>Standard deviation of peripapillary RNFL thickness across the TSNIT profile.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">visual-field-static-perimetry<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-visual-field-static-perimetry\"> </a></td><td>Automated static perimetry (visual field)</td><td>Panel code for an automated static threshold perimetry exam (e.g. Humphrey Field Analyzer).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">visual-field-test-pattern<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-visual-field-test-pattern\"> </a></td><td>Visual field test pattern</td><td>Pattern of tested points (e.g. 24-2, 30-2, 10-2, Esterman).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">visual-field-mean-deviation<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-visual-field-mean-deviation\"> </a></td><td>Visual field mean deviation (MD)</td><td>Weighted average deviation of measured threshold sensitivity from age-corrected normal values, in dB.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">visual-field-pattern-standard-deviation<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-visual-field-pattern-standard-deviation\"> </a></td><td>Visual field pattern standard deviation (PSD)</td><td>Index of localized sensitivity loss (non-uniformity of the deviation from normal), in dB.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">visual-field-index<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-visual-field-index\"> </a></td><td>Visual field index (VFI)</td><td>Global index of visual function expressed as a percentage of age-normal field.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">visual-field-screening-mode<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-visual-field-screening-mode\"> </a></td><td>Visual field screening test mode</td><td>Type of screening test mode used.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">visual-field-fixation-strategy<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-visual-field-fixation-strategy\"> </a></td><td>Visual field fixation strategy</td><td>Method used to monitor patient fixation (e.g. blind spot monitoring, gaze tracking).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">perimetry-stimulus-size<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-perimetry-stimulus-size\"> </a></td><td>Perimetry stimulus size</td><td>Size of the test stimulus (e.g. Goldmann III).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">perimetry-stimulus-color<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-perimetry-stimulus-color\"> </a></td><td>Perimetry stimulus color</td><td>Color of the test stimulus light.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">perimetry-background-luminance<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-perimetry-background-luminance\"> </a></td><td>Perimetry background luminance</td><td>Luminance of the perimeter bowl background (standard 31.5 asb).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">perimetry-max-stimulus-luminance<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-perimetry-max-stimulus-luminance\"> </a></td><td>Perimetry maximum stimulus luminance</td><td>Maximum luminance of the test stimulus.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">perimetry-stimulus-duration<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-perimetry-stimulus-duration\"> </a></td><td>Perimetry stimulus presentation time</td><td>Presentation time of each stimulus (standard 200 ms).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">visual-field-horizontal-extent<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-visual-field-horizontal-extent\"> </a></td><td>Visual field horizontal extent</td><td>Horizontal extent of the tested visual field, in degrees.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">visual-field-vertical-extent<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-visual-field-vertical-extent\"> </a></td><td>Visual field vertical extent</td><td>Vertical extent of the tested visual field, in degrees.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">visual-field-shape<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-visual-field-shape\"> </a></td><td>Visual field shape</td><td>Shape of the tested visual field (circle or rectangle).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">foveal-sensitivity<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-foveal-sensitivity\"> </a></td><td>Foveal threshold sensitivity</td><td>Threshold sensitivity measured at the fovea, in dB.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">visual-field-test-duration<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-visual-field-test-duration\"> </a></td><td>Visual field test duration</td><td>Total duration of the visual field test.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">visual-field-test-point-count<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-visual-field-test-point-count\"> </a></td><td>Number of visual field test points</td><td>Total number of points tested; depends on the test pattern.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">correction-lens-power<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-correction-lens-power\"> </a></td><td>Correction lens power</td><td>Spherical power of the trial/correction lens used during the test, in diopters.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">fixating-eye<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-fixating-eye\"> </a></td><td>Fixating eye</td><td>The eye that was fixating the target during the measurement. Answer is the eye (e.g. SNOMED CT 24028007 Right / 7771000 Left).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">strabismus-exam<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-strabismus-exam\"> </a></td><td>Strabismus examination</td><td>Panel code for a strabismus examination grouping whichever sub-tests were performed (cover test, motility, near point of convergence, stereopsis, prism cover test, Krimsky, etc.) via hasMember.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">cover-test<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-cover-test\"> </a></td><td>Cover test</td><td>Cover test (cover-uncover and/or alternate cover) assessing the presence and type of manifest or latent ocular deviation.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">ocular-motility<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-ocular-motility\"> </a></td><td>Ocular motility assessment</td><td>Assessment of extraocular muscle function (e.g. hypofunction or hyperfunction) of a specific muscle of one eye.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">near-point-of-convergence<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-near-point-of-convergence\"> </a></td><td>Near point of convergence</td><td>Near point of convergence (PPC), recorded as a distance in centimetres or as a qualitative finding.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">convergence-assessment<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-convergence-assessment\"> </a></td><td>Convergence assessment</td><td>Qualitative assessment of convergence ability (e.g. good, fair, insufficient, poor).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">stereopsis-test<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-stereopsis-test\"> </a></td><td>Stereopsis test</td><td>Stereoacuity test result (e.g. Titmus, Randot), qualitative or in seconds of arc.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">prism-cover-test<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-prism-cover-test\"> </a></td><td>Prism cover test</td><td>Panel code for a prism cover test measuring ocular deviation in prism diopters across one or more gaze positions.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">krimsky-test<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-krimsky-test\"> </a></td><td>Krimsky test</td><td>Panel code for a Krimsky test (corneal light reflex centred with prisms) measuring ocular deviation in prism diopters across one or more gaze positions.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">hirschberg-test<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-hirschberg-test\"> </a></td><td>Hirschberg test</td><td>Panel code for a Hirschberg corneal light reflex test estimating the angle of deviation across one or more gaze positions.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">red-filter-light-test<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-red-filter-light-test\"> </a></td><td>Red filter plus light test</td><td>Panel code for a red filter plus light test assessing fusion, suppression or diplopia across one or more gaze positions.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">worth-4-dot-test<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-worth-4-dot-test\"> </a></td><td>Worth 4 dot test</td><td>Panel code for a Worth 4 dot test assessing fusion, suppression or diplopia across one or more gaze positions.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">gaze-position-measurement<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-gaze-position-measurement\"> </a></td><td>Gaze position measurement</td><td>A single measurement or finding taken at one gaze position (e.g. primary position, right gaze) within a prism cover, Krimsky, Hirschberg, red filter or Worth 4 dot test.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">extraocular-muscle<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-extraocular-muscle\"> </a></td><td>Extraocular muscle assessed</td><td>The extraocular muscle being assessed (one of the four rectus or two oblique muscles). Answer is a CodeableConcept naming the muscle.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">extraocular-muscle-function<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-extraocular-muscle-function\"> </a></td><td>Extraocular muscle function</td><td>Functional finding for the assessed extraocular muscle (e.g. normal, hypofunction, hyperfunction).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">stereopsis-test-type<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-stereopsis-test-type\"> </a></td><td>Stereopsis test type</td><td>Which stereoacuity test was used (e.g. Titmus fly, Randot, Lang, TNO); affects interpretation of the result.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">horizontal-deviation<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-horizontal-deviation\"> </a></td><td>Horizontal ocular deviation</td><td>Magnitude of the horizontal ocular deviation at a gaze position, always a positive magnitude, in prism diopters (or degrees for a Hirschberg estimate); the direction (eso/exo) is recorded separately.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">vertical-deviation<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-vertical-deviation\"> </a></td><td>Vertical ocular deviation</td><td>Magnitude of the vertical ocular deviation at a gaze position, always a positive magnitude, in prism diopters; the direction (hyper/hypo) is recorded separately.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">gaze-position<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-gaze-position\"> </a></td><td>Gaze position</td><td>The gaze position (direction of gaze) at which a strabismus measurement was taken, e.g. primary position, right gaze, up-and-right gaze.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">gaze-position-finding<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-gaze-position-finding\"> </a></td><td>Finding at gaze position</td><td>Qualitative finding at a gaze position (e.g. Hirschberg reflex displacement, fusion, suppression or diplopia on red filter or Worth 4 dot testing).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">within-normal-limits<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-within-normal-limits\"> </a></td><td>Within normal limits</td><td>The measurement or analysis falls within the normal range of the device normative (age-matched reference) database (typically p &gt;= 5%).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">borderline<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-borderline\"> </a></td><td>Borderline</td><td>The measurement or analysis falls in the borderline range of the device normative database (typically 1% &lt;= p &lt; 5%).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">outside-normal-limits<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-outside-normal-limits\"> </a></td><td>Outside normal limits</td><td>The measurement or analysis falls outside the normal range of the device normative database (typically p &lt; 1%).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">rnfl-thickness-superior<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-rnfl-thickness-superior\"> </a></td><td>RNFL average thickness, superior quadrant</td><td>Average peripapillary retinal nerve fiber layer thickness in the superior quadrant of the circumpapillary scan.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">rnfl-thickness-inferior<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-rnfl-thickness-inferior\"> </a></td><td>RNFL average thickness, inferior quadrant</td><td>Average peripapillary retinal nerve fiber layer thickness in the inferior quadrant of the circumpapillary scan.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">rnfl-thickness-nasal<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-rnfl-thickness-nasal\"> </a></td><td>RNFL average thickness, nasal quadrant</td><td>Average peripapillary retinal nerve fiber layer thickness in the nasal quadrant of the circumpapillary scan.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">rnfl-thickness-temporal<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-rnfl-thickness-temporal\"> </a></td><td>RNFL average thickness, temporal quadrant</td><td>Average peripapillary retinal nerve fiber layer thickness in the temporal quadrant of the circumpapillary scan.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">glaucoma-hemifield-test<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-glaucoma-hemifield-test\"> </a></td><td>Glaucoma Hemifield Test result</td><td>Result of the Glaucoma Hemifield Test, comparing mirror-image superior and inferior sectors of the visual field (within normal limits, borderline, outside normal limits, general reduction of sensitivity, abnormally high sensitivity).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">fixation-losses<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-fixation-losses\"> </a></td><td>Fixation losses</td><td>Number of fixation losses (responses to stimuli presented in the physiological blind spot) relative to the number of fixation checks performed.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">false-positive-errors<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-false-positive-errors\"> </a></td><td>False positive errors</td><td>Percentage of false positive responses (responses without a stimulus being presented); a reliability index of the visual field test.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">false-negative-errors<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-false-negative-errors\"> </a></td><td>False negative errors</td><td>Percentage of false negative responses (no response to a supra-threshold stimulus at a previously seen location); a reliability index of the visual field test.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">test-distance-category<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-test-distance-category\"> </a></td><td>Testing distance category (near/far)</td><td>Categorical testing distance (near or far) at which a strabismus or binocular vision test was performed. Answer is a CodeableConcept (near / far). Distinct from test-distance, which records the testing distance as a Quantity.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">near<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-near\"> </a></td><td>Near</td><td>Near testing distance, approximately 33-40 cm.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">far<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-far\"> </a></td><td>Far</td><td>Far (distance) testing distance, approximately 6 m (20 ft).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">horizontal-deviation-direction<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-horizontal-deviation-direction\"> </a></td><td>Horizontal deviation direction</td><td>Direction of the horizontal ocular deviation at a gaze position (esodeviation, exodeviation, or orthophoria when no horizontal deviation is present). The magnitude is recorded separately as a positive value in horizontal-deviation.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">vertical-deviation-direction<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-vertical-deviation-direction\"> </a></td><td>Vertical deviation direction</td><td>Direction of the vertical ocular deviation of the deviating eye at a gaze position (hyperdeviation or hypodeviation). The magnitude is recorded separately as a positive value in vertical-deviation.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">esodeviation<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-esodeviation\"> </a></td><td>Esodeviation</td><td>Inward (nasal) horizontal deviation of the eye; covers esotropia and esophoria.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">exodeviation<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-exodeviation\"> </a></td><td>Exodeviation</td><td>Outward (temporal) horizontal deviation of the eye; covers exotropia and exophoria.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">orthophoria<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-orthophoria\"> </a></td><td>Orthophoria</td><td>Absence of any manifest or latent ocular deviation; the visual axes remain aligned under cover testing.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">hyperdeviation<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-hyperdeviation\"> </a></td><td>Hyperdeviation</td><td>Upward vertical deviation of the deviating eye relative to the fellow eye; covers hypertropia and hyperphoria.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">hypodeviation<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-hypodeviation\"> </a></td><td>Hypodeviation</td><td>Downward vertical deviation of the deviating eye relative to the fellow eye; covers hypotropia and hypophoria.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">fusion<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-fusion\"> </a></td><td>Fusion</td><td>Sensory fusion: the images of both eyes are combined into a single percept (e.g. a single pinkish light on the red filter plus light test, four lights on the Worth 4 dot test). SNOMED CT 78513008 Fusion binocular vision is an observable entity, not a finding, so it is not used as an answer.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-reflex-centered<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-reflex-centered\"> </a></td><td>Corneal light reflex centered</td><td>On corneal light reflex (Hirschberg) testing, the reflex is centered on the pupil of the eye assessed, consistent with no manifest deviation of that eye.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-reflex-displaced-nasal<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-reflex-displaced-nasal\"> </a></td><td>Corneal light reflex displaced nasally</td><td>On corneal light reflex (Hirschberg) testing, the reflex in the eye assessed is displaced nasally from the pupil centre, indicating an exodeviation of that eye.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-reflex-displaced-temporal<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-reflex-displaced-temporal\"> </a></td><td>Corneal light reflex displaced temporally</td><td>On corneal light reflex (Hirschberg) testing, the reflex in the eye assessed is displaced temporally from the pupil centre, indicating an esodeviation of that eye.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-reflex-displaced-superior<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-reflex-displaced-superior\"> </a></td><td>Corneal light reflex displaced superiorly</td><td>On corneal light reflex (Hirschberg) testing, the reflex in the eye assessed is displaced superiorly from the pupil centre, indicating a hypodeviation of that eye.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">corneal-reflex-displaced-inferior<a name=\"fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-reflex-displaced-inferior\"> </a></td><td>Corneal light reflex displaced inferiorly</td><td>On corneal light reflex (Hirschberg) testing, the reflex in the eye assessed is displaced inferiorly from the pupil centre, indicating a hyperdeviation of that eye.</td></tr></table></div>"
  ] ;
